    thinking: "**Expanding the App Concept**\n\nI\'m now considering how to expand the app\'s features based on the recent input about a calendar-like view for children. The idea is to integrate task assignments and point tracking into this view, enabling children to easily visualize their progress. Moreover, I\'m thinking about empowering parents with the ability to assign these tasks within the same framework.\n\n\n**Refining the Interface Design**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user interface, and I\'m leaning toward a toggle system. It will switch between \"Parent Mode\" and \"Kids Mode\". In the latter, the child will see a week-based calendar, showing behavior points and tasks for each day. Clicking a day reveals behavior stars and a checklist of tasks. The main idea is interactivity and elegance, aiming for a visual representation of progress.\n\n\n**Defining Task Structures**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the task structure. My aim is a robust system tied to the weekly grid. Each task will include a unique ID, a title, assigned days (as an array of day indices), and points earned upon completion. I\'m focusing on simplicity and flexibility, with an internal `completedDays` tracker mapping tasks to their weekly completion.\n\n\n"
