ion, deletion, and completion toggles. I\'m verifying the current structure and functionality to ensure the new functions integrate seamlessly.\n\n\n**Initializing Task Array**\n\nI\'m now focusing on initializing the `tasks` array for existing children in `window.localStorage`. I\'m going to implement lazy initialization to handle cases where the array might be missing, using `child.tasks || []`. Next, I will write state update handlers for adding and deleting tasks for children, with an emphasis on adding a toast message upon task assignment.\n\n\n**Refining Task Deletion**\n\nI\'ve just finished refining the `deleteTask` function, integrating it with the children state management. I\'m leveraging `prevChildren` for immutability, ensuring that tasks are removed effectively, and updating the state accordingly. I\'m also including `addToast` functionality to give a concise and instant feedback confirmation.\n\n```javascript\n    import { useCallback } from \'react\';\n\n  const deleteTask = useCallback((childId: string, taskId:\n  ```\n\n**Adding Audio Feedback**\n\nI\'m now integrating an `AudioContext` within a `playCompletionSound` function to give audio feedback for task completion, specifically for happy chimes. I\'m testing the function and refining the implementation for broader browser compatibility. I\'m working to minimize any console warnings.\n\n\n**Designing the Parent View**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Vista Padres\" design, starting with tab selection for `ChildCard` with \"Vista Padres \360\237\221\221\" as default. This view allows for editing behavior stars, adding review comments for AI feedback, and now summarizing completed tasks. I\'m also planning the \"Asignador de Tareas\" with form, pre-selected and active task lists for parents. This layout integrates seamlessly with the new functionality.\n\n\n**Visualizing Day Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the day view, which begins when a child selects a calendar day. I\'m designing a focused view including a large card displaying the day name with a calendar emoji. I am also working on designing conduct star displays, and interactive tasks that indicate completion with visual and auditory feedback. Then a child-friendly summary of points earned for the day.\n\n\n"
