  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Child Card Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on redesigning `components/ChildCard.tsx`. My primary goal is to incorporate two tabs: \"Vista Padres \360\237\221\221\" and \"Vista Calendario \360\237\223\205\". I\'m leaning towards setting the default view to either \"Vista Calendario \360\237\223\205\" or \"Vista Padres \360\237\221\221\".\n\n\n**Calculating Child Points**\n\nI\'ve shifted my focus to calculating points and incorporating a \"Vista Calendario \360\237\223\205\" or \"Vista Padres \360\237\221\221\" toggle. I am implementing a segment control under the child\'s name using state: `const [activeMode, setActiveMode] = useState<\'parents\' | \'kids\'>(\'kids\');`. I am also now checking `child.scores` to determine points! It looks like points are calculated as the sum of behavior stars (1-5) and task points.\n\n\n**Refining Point Calculation**\n\nI\'ve refined the point calculation, ensuring each completed task on assigned days contributes. I\'m now displaying \"Total Points: X (\342\255\220 Y stars + \360\237\217\206 Z tasks)\" which I think is very clear. I\'m also preparing to build a task assignment form for the \"Vista Padres \360\237\221\221\" view. This form will allow parents to assign new tasks, defining the task name and selecting the days.\n\n\n**Designing Task Assignment**\n\nI\'m now designing the task assignment form for the parent\'s view. I\'m focusing on a weekly task assignment interface. I\'m storing selected days in an array of indices with toggleable functionality. A \"Seleccionar todos\" helper is included for convenience! There\'s a point selector and a \"Asignar Tarea\" button. I\'m also preparing the display of the active task list.\nI need to show an informative message if no tasks are assigned yet.\nThen I need to show each assigned task, days assigned, points value, and a remove button.\nAfter, I need to show the weekly behavior stars grid with an AI feedback generator and history.\nFinally, I will create the \"Vista Calendario \360\237\223\205\" (Child View), with a weekly agenda tracker or modern \"bento\" calendar row. Each day displays the day name and rating.\n\n\n**Developing Calendar Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the daily calendar detail view for the child\'s perspective. I\'m focusing on displaying conduct status using stars or a dash. I\'m also adding a mini-progress indicator for tasks like \"\360\237\237\242\" for all done, or \"1/3\". Clicking a day sets the active calendar day, displaying details in a focused card. It shows the selected day name and conduct stars. I\'m handling task display too.\n\n\n**Implementing Daily Achievement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a delightful, child-friendly display for daily achievements. I plan to integrate a progress bar or a circle indicator showing today\'s progress. I\'ll also dynamically calculate and display \"Total points achieved today\" including behavior stars and completed tasks, and include a celebratory banner \"\360\237\217\206 \302\241D\303\255a Perfecto! \302\241Cumpliste todas tus metas hoy! \360\237\214\237\" if all tasks are complete. I am also preparing the import and incorporation of various `lucide-react` icons to elevate the visual appeal of the calendar and task assignment layout. I will be sure to examine `ChildCard.tsx` and related dependencies.\n\n\n**Refactoring Imports and Sound**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a code cleanup pass. I am prioritizing import organization and writing sound playback in `ChildCard.tsx` itself. I\'m defining a function for a delightful audio cue for task completion, ensuring proper `useEffect` usage to avoid any infinite loops during audio context creation.\n\n\n**Designing Task Pre-selection**\n\nI\'m now integrating a list of pre-selected standard tasks to streamline the task assignment process. This will simplify task creation for parents; they can simply select from a list! I\'m also refining the day selection feature in the parent task assignment form, including \"Todos los d\303\255as,\" \"Lunes a viernes,\" and \"Fin de semana\" buttons for easy day selection.\n\n\n**Constructing Card Component**\n\nI\'m now focusing on reconstructing the complete `ChildCard.tsx` component, ensuring all props are correctly implemented. I\'m double-checking imports and adding Lucide icons. I am constructing the task assignment form, and point selections of 1, 2, 3, or 5 points. I am also working on the \"Asignar Tarea\" button, too!\n\n\n**Reviewing Icon Integration**\n\nI\'m now reviewing icon usage, comparing existing custom icons with Lucide equivalents for consistency and aesthetics. I plan to seamlessly integrate the most suitable icons. I\'m checking `components/icons.tsx` to identify used icons. I\'ll thoughtfully draft `/components/ChildCard.tsx` to ensure elegance and robustness. Additionally, I\'ll ensure task completion triggers the `playCompletionSound` function.\n\n\n**Designing Calendar Row**\n\nI\'m now focused on the \"Vista Calendario \360\237\223\205\" layout. The weekly calendar row has a clear title and seven day cards. Each card displays the day name, conduct stars, and a task completion progress badge. The selected day is visually distinct with a shadow and border. Below, there\'s a detailed view with the day\'s name and conduct stars.\n\n\n**Displaying Task Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the daily task display within the calendar. I\'m dynamically generating the task list for the selected day, showing a clear check button for each task. The button toggles the task completion state, providing immediate visual feedback through animations or strike-through text and visual badges. If no tasks are assigned, a celebratory message \"\302\241No tienes tareas asignadas para el Martes! \360\237\216\211\" is displayed.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will update `/components/ChildCard.tsx` by writing a complete, beautifully redesigned implementation. It will include a dual toggle for parent management and kid interactive calendar modes, a browser-synth chime sound upon completing tasks, suggested task quick-chips, a weekly calendar navigation layout, and rewards tracking."
