    thinking: "**Simplifying the Star System**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core of this request. The goal is a streamlined system, moving away from a 1-to-5 star rating and toward something simpler. It\'s a binary choice. It is a simplified checklist. It is a selector for daily actions. The focus is to make it faster for users to rate behaviors.\n\n\n**Refining the Rating System**\n\nI\'ve got the scoring system almost finalized. The revised system uses 1.0, 0.5, 0, -0.5, and -1.0 stars. I\'m focusing on the implementation details now, especially within the code. Currently, `child.scores` is an array of numbers representing 7 days. I\'m checking how the decimal values will be stored and rendered in `/components/ChildCard.tsx` and verifying the data types in `/types.ts`. I am confident that scores can handle these values.\n\n\n**Evaluating Icon Representation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual representation, specifically icons, for the simplified rating system. My goal is to determine which existing icons best suit the new \"1 Star\" and \"0 (Neutral)\" states. I\'m exploring `/components/icons.tsx` and the `lucide-react` imports to assess available options. I\'m examining `/components/StarRating.tsx` to understand current usage and find the best icon to replace or represent the rating.\n\n\n**Implementing the Scoring**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to score behaviors using half-stars and demerits. I will focus on implementing a half star, or media estrella, for a positive behavior that is less than perfect. I\'m also thinking how the code, specifically the `onUpdateScore` callback in `/components/ChildCard.tsx`, will handle this.\n\n\n**Analyzing StarRating\'s Usage**\n\nI\'m currently confirming the application of the `StarRating` component. I see the function is used in both the child and parent review sections, each within `ChildCard.tsx`. This component must be updated so it handles the rating selection system, and also updated the visual representation of this.\n\n\n**Designing the New Selector**\n\nI am now visualizing the implementation. I\'ve designed the selector to have four distinct choices. It will consist of buttons, or maybe segments, with icons and labels, perfectly suiting the \"1 estrella\", \"media estrella\", and \"demerito\" requirements. I\'ve thought about how it will appear on mobile and desktop views, with clear labels and icons. I plan to use the icons as the visual indicator in `/components/ChildCard.tsx`. I believe the design is now elegant and functional!\n\n\n**Adapting Visual Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on adapting the visual display of the ratings. The existing 5-star rendering needs an update because we\'re using scores of `1.0`, `0.5`, `0`, and `-1.0`. I\'m going to look at how `grandTotalPoints` and `totalBehaviorStars` are calculated, particularly in the context of the new scoring system. My goal is to find a way to make it still look like it\'s stars being given and taken!\n\n\n"
