  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Display Location**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the best place to display the sweet progress bar within the \"Kids\" view. I\'m leaning toward positioning it near the \"Calendario Semanal\" calendar card when `activeMode` is \'kids\'. Thinking through specific placements, it seems like before or after the card might work well, I\'m now referencing lines 2 for consideration.\n\n\n**Defining Sweet Visual**\n\nI\'ve decided the \"Kids\" view is the ideal location and am designing a \"Weekly Sweet Goal\" section right there. This sweet card will showcase progress: \"\302\241Meta Semanal de Dulce!\" with current points (e.g., `45 / 50 puntos`). A vibrant progress bar with a gradient (considering amber/pink/red, pink/amber, or purple/pink) will be visually key, culminating in a candy icon or treasure chest at 100%. A celebratory banner will appear upon reaching the sweet goal.\n\n\n**Refining Celebration Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the celebratory elements. I\'m imagining a vibrant banner that reads \"\302\241HAS GANADO TU DULCE DE LA SEMANA! \360\237\215\254\360\237\215\255\" with a pulse animation and sparkles. I\'m envisioning playful confetti effects. Ideally, the candy icon would be interactive, perhaps with a shake or heartbeat animation on click. The customization aspect is important in Parents mode, where they can set the goal.\n\n\n**Defining Child Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided callbacks to enhance child management. I\'m focusing on the `ChildCard` component and how it will handle updates. I\'m working with the `onUpdateScore`, `onRemoveChild`, `onUpdateAvatar`, `onAddFeedback`, `onAddTask`, `onDeleteTask`, `onToggleTask`, and `onUpdatePointsGoal` callbacks to implement user actions directly on the ChildCard. I\'m calculating and displaying progress as well.\n\n\n**Implementing Progress Bar**\n\nI\'m now implementing the progress bar in the `ChildCard` component within the \"Kids\" view, specifically at line 264 of `ChildCard.tsx`.  I\'ve added the code inside the existing `<div>` element, right after the mode check, and am making sure it\'s visually appealing with a gradient background and ambient sparkles.  I\'m also working on calculating and displaying the current points and goal within the bar\'s interface.\n\n\n**Refining Candy Icons**\n\nI\'m now optimizing the candy icon display within the `ChildCard`. I\'ve added a bounce animation to the candy emoji and I\'m refining the title and subtitle to be more engaging. The plan is to create a dynamic call to action to motivate the children to achieve their sweet weekly goal. I\'ve also incorporated the point display as well.\n\n\n**Optimizing Progress Bar**\n\nI\'m now refining the progress bar\'s visual elements within the ChildCard. Specifically, I\'m working to make the colored fill more dynamic and visually interesting by incorporating a stripe effect and a shiny animation for a more dynamic feel. I am referencing line 3 of the source code. I\'m also ensuring the bar\'s gradient flows smoothly, and the calculations are accurate.\n\n\n**Integrating Candy Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating the candy icon\'s final resting position as an absolute element within the progress bar, dynamically calculated based on the `progressPercent`. I\'m using `isGoalReached` to apply a drop shadow and a pulse animation on the candy when the sweet goal is met. The candy icon\'s left positioning is linked directly to the progress completion percentage.\n\n\n**Finalizing Visual Feedback**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for when the sweet goal is reached, particularly focusing on the display for the `isGoalReached` state. I\'ve designed a celebratory panel with a joyful animation and text. This panel displays when the goal is met and provides encouraging feedback, alongside visual elements. I\'m referencing the code snippet for reference.\n\n\n\n**Refining Animation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the progress bar animation, debating between stripes or a smooth gradient. I\'m leaning toward a robust gradient but also want an added, premium touch. I\'ll explore adding a pulsing effect on hover or scale. I need to make sure I add this in tailwind or CSS.\nI\'m also identifying where the parents view customization is located, referencing lines 453-455.\n\n\n**Adding Configuration Block**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a \"Meta de Puntos para el Dulce Semanal\" configuration block within the Parents view, positioned before the daily ratings grid, specifically to lines 453-455. The configuration is meant to allow customization of the candy reward point goal. I\'ve designed the UI with a gradient background and a candy icon to make it visually engaging. This section should include an explanation of the goal.\n\n\n**Implementing Input Controls**\n\nI\'m now implementing the input controls for customizing the sweet goal within the Parent\'s view, referencing the code snippet for the preset buttons and the input label. I\'m focusing on making the interaction intuitive and user-friendly, ensuring a clear display of the current point goal. I\'m making sure it is responsive, and clear for use.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration Display**\n\nI\'m now refining the display of the configuration block in Parents view, specifically the custom amount input. I am focusing on input validation and visual feedback to enhance the user experience. The interaction must be refined to support preset buttons and the input label. I\'m ensuring proper min/max values are supported.\n\n\n**Verifying ChildCard Updates**\n\nI\'m now verifying the integration of `onUpdatePointsGoal` within the `ChildCard` component. I\'ve confirmed its correct placement within the function signature, ensuring it aligns with other callbacks. I\'m double-checking the import statements and the internal handling of this callback to ensure seamless function calls. I\'m focusing on lines 70 to 80, ensuring no existing functions are disrupted.\n\n\n"
